      "fullContent": "Emad on X: \"Landmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\" / X Post\nLog in Sign up\nPost\nEmad on X: \"Landmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\"\nEmad\n@EMostaque\nLandmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\nOpenAI\n@OpenAI\n12h\nWe’re sharing a solution to the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem, one of the deepest problems at the frontier of mathematics.\nThe proof was produced by a group of agents, using an OpenAI next-generation model significantly more capable than GPT-6 Astra.\nThe problem Show more\n17:35 · 2026年9月8日 1.3万 Views\n16\n3\n171\n16\nEmad\n@EMostaque\nLandmark event on the way to ASI, congratulations to the team\nJust because one solution showing blow up has been found doesn't mean there aren't more out there!\nAlso RIP my codex\nOpenAI\n@OpenAI\n12h\nWe’re sharing a solution to the Navier-Stokes Millennium Prize Problem, one of the deepest problems at the frontier of mathematics.\nThe proof was produced by a group of agents, using an OpenAI next-generation model significantly more capable than GPT-6 Astra.\nThe problem Show more\n17:35 · 2026年9月8日 1.3万 Views\n16\n3\n171\n16\nRand\n@rand_longevity\n12h\nyep this is one of the moments\n2\n180\ncarlos\n@carloslondrez\n11h\nThe most surprising thing is the comments on the announcement post. The labs really need to cure some major diseases ASAP.\n1\n66\nTimmo Nielsen 🇸🇪 e/acc, L/0\n@timmo_nielsen\n10h\nPpl are saying Openai Stole the info from Antropic. :/ hahaha\n1\n21"
