      "fullContent": "Greg Brockman on X: \"arc-agi-3 is now saturated\" / X Post\nLog in Sign up\nPost\nGreg Brockman on X: \"arc-agi-3 is now saturated\"\nGreg Brockman\n@gdb\narc-agi-3 is now saturated\nARC Prize\n@arcprize\n9月3日\nGPT-6 Astra by @ OpenAI achieves SOTA on ARC-AGI:\n- Astra scores 63% on ARC-AGI-3, 99% via a new provider adapter harness\n- It surpasses human performance on 96% of ARC-AGI-3 levels\n- It builds the most precise symbolic model of novel environments we've seen\nOur analysis:\n21:46 · 2026年9月3日 21.2万 Views\n124\n122\n2977\n158\nGreg Brockman\n@gdb\narc-agi-3 is now saturated\nARC Prize\n@arcprize\n9月3日\nGPT-6 Astra by @ OpenAI achieves SOTA on ARC-AGI:\n- Astra scores 63% on ARC-AGI-3, 99% via a new provider adapter harness\n- It surpasses human performance on 96% of ARC-AGI-3 levels\n- It builds the most precise symbolic model of novel environments we've seen\nOur analysis:\n21:46 · 2026年9月3日 21.2万 Views\n124\n122\n2977\n158\nBraden\n@vxbe_dev\n9月3日\nWould love to verify it, but you guys are choosing who get's access to intelligence giving select companies a MASSIVE benefit compared to those who don't have access. It's horrible, and in my mind directly goes against Openai's stated goals.\n4\n26\n2492\nBeff (e/acc)\n@beffjezos\n9月3日\ngg\n19\n1737\nsamir\n@samirettali\n9月4日\nwell, that was quick\n1\n15\n907"
